{"title":"1993 USAMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For each integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/a/39abfe232e2ed5247aa4028089e5f651090e66da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />, determine, with proof, which of the two positive real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> satisfying\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a63b2ade70110e8161ea351e1b94044db3fc522.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^n=a+1,\\qquad b^{2n}=b+3a\\]\" width=\"221\" height=\"18\" />\nis larger.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>First, note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/7/117ebb483f58d8ef29841cafed8f31e86952daf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, since otherwise <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/7/b57563814e8191f50f2249578b9c2a914def4a6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^n-a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/1/87101bdae19a9c58ffd4445708c7cb13921f2dde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^{2n}-b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" /> would be nonpositive. Then, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/0/6d0d144606dacc344c49b3e598fce7a994fd7e3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=x^{2n}-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"120\" height=\"21\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is strictly increasing on the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/3/e639292c6bac8afec032be76b34b4505b4e249c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, \\infty)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"18\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/0/e60b4e4601a638b23649d2f655a861363dac7582.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} (a-1)^2&gt;0 \\implies a^2+2a+1&gt;4a \\implies a^{2n}&gt;4a \\\\  \\implies a^{2n}-a&gt;3a \\implies f(a)&gt; 3a = f(b) \\implies a&gt; b &amp;&amp; \\square \\end{align*}\" width=\"462\" height=\"47\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Square and rearrange the first equation and also rearrange the second.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/c/31cef189a8ef7c90b6464e786c80090214de0d30.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align} a^{2n}-a&amp;=a^2+a+1\\\\ b^{2n}-b&amp;=3a \\end{align}\" width=\"319\" height=\"46\" />\nIt is <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Trivial_Inequality\" title=\"Trivial Inequality\">trivial</a> that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/0/360198e5608aa3823c3d33ed5fd678bd601c4a36.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} (a-1)^2 &gt; 0 \\tag{3} \\end{align*}\" width=\"285\" height=\"19\" />\nsince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/6/cc6873715a60ff7706da71b8cad30cead78b1ad3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> clearly cannot equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (Otherwise <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/9/ff905825e006b2f1d3ec80eba093e25ca872c01a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^n=1\\neq 1+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"17\" />).  Thus\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/d/6ed900a9db67fe8739ae9db3160f80b3f8bbe7c2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} a^2+a+1&amp;&gt;3a \\tag{4}\\\\ a^{2n}-a&amp;&gt;b^{2n}-b \\tag{5} \\end{align*}\" width=\"317\" height=\"46\" />\nwhere we substituted in equations (1) and (2) to achieve (5).  Notice that from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/a/a2a5524006ab541e7da8acb082871550bac81d43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{n}=a+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"86\" height=\"16\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb8726d98aced2f3140dd77a2d8614c2e7674700.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />.  Thus, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/f/9dfc685c058a3923bc44dc7a591ea65066c69dea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&gt;a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/e/fee1d8875ebdde90dac4d7e8ee153115ff345e31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^{2n-1}-1&gt;a^{2n-1}-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"168\" height=\"15\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/d/34dfdc995c0e009488895f13ce003d35fc5d7474.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;1\\Rightarrow a^{2n-1}-1&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"177\" height=\"15\" />, multiplying the two inequalities yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/8/73825151ceb45d78beb3b59bac5affc1927e46ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^{2n}-b&gt;a^{2n}-a$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"134\" height=\"15\" />, a contradiction, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/4/4d4078e0d09ff1c45c862287e802a524d5a8bfc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt; b$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />.  However, when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the first equation becomes meaningless, so we conclude that for each integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/a/39abfe232e2ed5247aa4028089e5f651090e66da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />, we always have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/2/082852571ecc48ed136ba13dcffa8f6e40064bbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8137713c2ee24695d4cfcc9c11ba408259a7db3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=x^n-x-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"142\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/2/5a2658d5ba2a3c8a04a9c409d5bca6cb61060cc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)=x^{2n}-x-3a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"157\" height=\"19\" />. By Descarte's Rule of Signs, both polynomials' only positive roots are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, respectively. With the Intermediate Value Theorem and the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/5/445140a0ab5a35a4023aaff14e008e1c70a77d8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1)=-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/9/b79e3c8fc7f2cbc779793776426477b466e61311.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2)=2^n-3&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"140\" height=\"18\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/f/2efcdcf07d2aaf302562d1114e387ff7e1d5e14c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\in(1,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />.\nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/d/bdd6fcdb63d79de781991e16e4f475e9efe416fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-3a\\in(-6,-3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"122\" height=\"18\" />, which means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/8/9c8a4e3e225e8c85f3f9d58e1664dffa8acf0cb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(1)=-3a&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"122\" height=\"18\" />. Also, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/7/0775f672a8f84d61395877186767707b64e1b33c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(a)=a^{2n}-4a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"19\" />. All that remains to prove is that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/b/c3b50156ff07ca0ba4a88c9e2b2dc33dbf989eb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(a)&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/3/953541844b2b95898a043f9335d361ecfcc6a610.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{2n}-4a&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"99\" height=\"15\" />. We can then conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> from the Intermediate Value Theorem. From the first equation given, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/8/7b8cca07082cebd11bdd4fbfe261e487d7462add.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{2n}=(a+1)^2=a^2+2a+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"224\" height=\"19\" />. Subtracting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/4/de4666d5b88a5a12f9055189db2a68e4135c67f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4a$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/8/5e8e2e815e6edbb07fdf7e45a6ee6ee60b34da72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2-2a+1&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"122\" height=\"16\" />, which is clearly true, as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/e/b0eb28666e3cbe3e4c173fb5b212c5ad539a3d50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\neq1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" />. Therefore, we conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/3/13360dba5e2837e754902b629f43459bf9a189dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1&lt;b&lt;a&lt;2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"107\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_USAMO\" title=\"1993 USAMO\">1993 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"1993 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1993\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Problem</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1993 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1993 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1993 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1993 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1993 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017072357\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.034 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.075 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 294/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1237/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 51/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9016/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   11.710      1 -total\n 55.83%    6.538      1 Template:USAMO_box\n 42.25%    4.947      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6608:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017072357 and revision id 283960. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}